    ns1:abstract "The view o f the author (Merritt.in Auton e / of.1990) is that the shelly cln).together with masses of shell.dianiicton occurring elseuhere in the vicinity (Peacock 1975).are indeed glacially transported allochthons probably derived from the Loch Ness Basin.which had been an arm of the sea prior to the build-up of the bate-Devensian ice-sheet A mean amino acid ratio of 0.04 has been obtained from Lr/rorincr.y originally collected from the \"Main Pit\" in I892 ( D .Q. Bowen.pers.comm.).As Li//oriritrs of lpswichian (stage 5e) age are known to have ratios of about 0.1, Bowen uould place the C-lava ratios more or less in the mid-Devensian.The probably infinite radiocarbon dates, houeier.suggest that the shelly clak is at least mid-Devensian in age.A mid to early-Devensian date is compatible Nith the faunal evidence (Graham. in Auton er ( I / 1990).uhich suggests that the clay formed in cold, rather than t'ull) xrctic conditions.Follouing the re-opening of the \"Main Pit'. in September 1990, fresh shell material has been submitted for lurthcr AMS and amino acid datlns. F r ~i n wLtrc. 1/11 Bori<./rerLakc sediment samples from t&o cores." ;
    ns1:doi "10.1111/j.1475-4754.1991.tb00691.x" .

